                <pb facs="0052" n="40" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg40"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.20 Defense/1432/4: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Jenkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-10-03T16:00:00-04:00">October 3, 1940—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>79. For General Strong from Major Taylor.</p>
                <p>“After numerous delays conversations with Bolivian Chief of Staff terminated
                    satisfactorily. Air photographs authorized using American equipment. Medical
                    mission approved. Leaving for Washington October 4.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jenkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
